{"t_ms": 8936, "event": {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011ChSmVNLxJHhPMa86UTDK7", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01NvrACPgQauA6bELp2XMDQC", "name": "Read", "input": {"file_path": "/private/var/folders/1b/0rzjfwh10r73w82mvb9k7h100000gn/T/patch-precedent-agent-gc7hj1um/relate/docs/adr/0580-post-release-workspace-versioning.md", "offset": 25, "limit": 20}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 913, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6097, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 913}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8eb3ecab-ac2b-4683-9a0d-f7d06503f11c", "uuid": "e56572ef-daad-4868-99d6-00df5c9d5954", "timestamp": "2026-11-27T04:02:39.303Z", "request_id": "req_011ChSmVNBY5VQDJc8EJxy6Y", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01NvrACPgQauA6bELp2XMDQC": {"file_path": "/private/var/folders/1b/0rzjfwh10r73w82mvb9k7h100000gn/T/patch-precedent-agent-gc7hj1um/relate/docs/adr/0580-post-release-workspace-versioning.md", "offset": 25, "limit": 20}}}}
{"t_ms": 8964, "event": {"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01NvrACPgQauA6bELp2XMDQC", "type": "tool_result", "content": "25\t\n26\t## Decision\n27\t\n28\tMain never carries a released version. The tagged release commit is\n29\tthe one transient carrier — it must hold the version it releases — and\n30\tthe same release run advances main past it: after each release the\n31\tworkspace advances to the next unreleased plain-semver version, no\n32\tpre-release marker. The advance is a release-bot step in release.yml,\n33\tperforming the version-surface sweep the bump performs without the\n34\tchangelog rotation — an advance is not a release cut, and rotating\n35\tthen would mint a release section for a version that never shipped —\n36\tso the released version exists only on the tagged commit and on the\n37\tregistries, and main's manifest stays disjoint from the published set.\n38\t\n39\tRegistry-consistent verification — checking that what the registries\n40\thold matches what the workspace declares — runs only in the release\n41\tpipeline's ordered publish, the one place the two are meant to agree.\n42\tIt is never a standing lane on main: between releases they are\n43\tdeliberately apart, so a main-based check would report the invariant\n44\titself as drift."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8eb3ecab-ac2b-4683-9a0d-f7d06503f11c", "uuid": "4c6e5ed0-179a-4f5a-b62e-780e7f1c1d04", "timestamp": "2026-11-27T04:02:39.332Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/private/var/folders/1b/0rzjfwh10r73w82mvb9k7h100000gn/T/patch-precedent-agent-gc7hj1um/relate/docs/adr/0580-post-release-workspace-versioning.md", "content": "\n## Decision\n\nMain never carries a released version. The tagged release commit is\nthe one transient carrier — it must hold the version it releases — and\nthe same release run advances main past it: after each release the\nworkspace advances to the next unreleased plain-semver version, no\npre-release marker. The advance is a release-bot step in release.yml,\nperforming the version-surface sweep the bump performs without the\nchangelog rotation — an advance is not a release cut, and rotating\nthen would mint a release section for a version that never shipped —\nso the released version exists only on the tagged commit and on the\nregistries, and main's manifest stays disjoint from the published set.\n\nRegistry-consistent verification — checking that what the registries\nhold matches what the workspace declares — runs only in the release\npipeline's ordered publish, the one place the two are meant to agree.\nIt is never a standing lane on main: between releases they are\ndeliberately apart, so a main-based check would report the invariant\nitself as drift.", "numLines": 20, "startLine": 25, "totalLines": 79}}}}
{"t_ms": 12407, "event": {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011ChSmVZfM8ts7obKbyF8eB", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The patch makes `release-bump.sh` rotate the changelog on every sweep, including the post-release advance. ADR-0580 says the advance performs the version-surface sweep \"without the changelog rotation\". Rotating at an advance \"would mint a release section for a version that never shipped\". The patch removes the `--skip-changelog` behaviour that enforced this.\n\nI did not run any tests. The test that guards this rule is in `scripts/tests/test_release_advance.sh`. It runs the bump with `--skip-changelog` on an empty-`[Unreleased]` changelog and checks the file is unchanged. With the patch, that run would rotate the changelog and the check would fail. That is my reading of the code, not an observed result.\n\n{\"verdict\": \"violates\", \"decisions\": [\"ADR-0580\"], \"checks\": [\"advance: empty-[Unreleased] CHANGELOG.md byte-identical — no heading inserted, [Unreleased] ref unchanged\"], \"check_outcomes\": {\"advance: empty-[Unreleased] CHANGELOG.md byte-identical — no heading inserted, [Unreleased] ref unchanged\": \"unknown\"}}"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 558, "cache_read_input_tokens": 7010, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 558}, "output_tokens": 384, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8eb3ecab-ac2b-4683-9a0d-f7d06503f11c", "uuid": "d5311867-9fa2-4dab-8f3a-93b4a68021d0", "timestamp": "2026-11-27T04:02:42.772Z", "request_id": "req_011ChSmVZWuVsaLpYNZxPbwo"}}
